0..77 Comment "// A theory\'s closed terms as a type, `Terms(S)`, and a fold out of them into"
78..108 Comment "// one of the theory\'s models."
109..111 Comment "//"
112..189 Comment "// A theory has models, `Model(S)`, and the initial one is its terms. Without"
190..263 Comment "// `Terms(S)` a source writes the theory twice: once as the signature its"
264..320 Comment "// models meet, and again as a data block for the terms."
321..323 Comment "//"
324..398 Comment "// `Terms(S)` derives one data declaration per theory, one constructor per"
399..472 Comment "// operation, named `S.op` in a term and in a pattern. The theory\'s rules"
473..549 Comment "// orient as the data block\'s own, and the block\'s presentation check judges"
550..613 Comment "// them. A fold into a model module respects that model\'s laws."
614..616 Comment "//"
617..695 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/theory-terms.gandr` — a monoid\'s terms, refused"
696..757 Comment "// - owes: #4148 — the terms as a model, and a derived fold"
758..804 Comment "// - owes: #4149 — a fold over a model value"
805..850 Comment "// - owes: #4150 — terms over several sorts"
851..931 Comment "// - see: `model/identity/loop-winding.gandr` — a fold out of a presented type"
932..956 Comment "//   into a model module"
